===Etymology===
From {{der|en|grc|ἔκζεμα}}, from {{m|grc|ἐκ||out of, forth from}} + {{m|grc|ζέμα||that which is boiled, decoction}}, from {{m|grc|ζέω||to boil, to seethe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛks.mə/|/ˈɛɡz.mə/|/ˈɛk.sɪ.mə/|/ˈɛɡ.zɪ.mə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɛɡ.zə.mə/|/ˈɛk.sə.mə/|/ɪɡ.ˈziː.mə/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ec|zem|a}}, {{hyphenation|en|ecze|ma|nocaption=1}}, {{hyphenation|en|ec|ze|ma|nocaption=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|eczemata|s}}

# A non-contagious acute or chronic [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by redness, itching, and the outbreak of oozing [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become encrusted and scaly.

